        "answerKey": "1. Let x be any point in U \\cap V. This means x is in U and x is in V.\n2. Since U is open and x is in U, there exists r1 > 0 such that the ball B(x, r1) is contained in U.\n3. Since V is open and x is in V, there exists r2 > 0 such that the ball B(x, r2) is contained in V.\n4. Choose r = min(r1, r2) > 0. Since r \\le r1, B(x, r) is contained in B(x, r1), hence B(x, r) is contained in U.\n5. Since r \\le r2, B(x, r) is contained in B(x, r2), hence B(x, r) is contained in V.\n6. Therefore, B(x, r) is contained in U \\cap V, which proves that U \\cap V is open."
