        "answerKey": "1. Definition: The boundary \\partial S of a set S is the set of points x in R^n such that every open ball centered at x contains at least one point in S and at least one point not in S (i.e. in the complement of S).\n2. Alternative: \\partial S = cl(S) \\setminus int(S), where cl(S) is the closure and int(S) is the interior of S.\n3. Closed Set Condition: A set S is closed if and only if it contains all of its boundary points, i.e., \\partial S is contained in S.\n4. Proof: S is closed <=> S = cl(S). Since cl(S) = S \\cup \\partial S, this equality holds if and only if \\partial S is contained in S."
