        "answerKey": "1. We evaluate the limit along different paths to (0,0):\n   Along the path y = mx^2:\n   lim_{(x,y)->(0,0)} f(x,y) = lim_{x->0} (x^2 * mx^2) / (x^4 + (mx^2)^2) = lim_{x->0} (m x^4) / (x^4(1 + m^2)) = m / (1 + m^2).\n2. This limit depends on the value of m (e.g. if m=1, limit is 1/2; if m=0, limit is 0).\n3. Since different paths yield different limit values, the double limit lim_{(x,y)->(0,0)} f(x,y) does not exist.\n4. Therefore, f is not continuous at (0,0)."
