        "id": 21,
        "question": "State Fubini's Theorem for double integrals over rectangular regions. Evaluate the integral $\\int_0^1 \\int_0^2 (x^2y + xy^2) \\, dy \\, dx$.",
        "answerKey": "1. Theorem: If f(x,y) is continuous on rectangular region R = [a,b] x [c,d], then the double integral of f over R equals the iterated integrals: \\iint_R f(x,y) dA = \\int_a^b \\int_c^d f(x,y) dy dx = \\int_c^d \\int_a^b f(x,y) dx dy.\n2. Evaluate inner integral w.r.t y:\n   \\int_0^2 (x^2y + xy^2) dy = [x^2 y^2 / 2 + x y^3 / 3]_0^2 = 2x^2 + 8x/3.\n3. Evaluate outer integral w.r.t x:\n   \\int_0^1 (2x^2 + 8x/3) dx = [2x^3 / 3 + 4x^2 / 3]_0^1 = 2/3 + 4/3 = 6/3 = 2."
