        "answerKey": "1. Green's Theorem: $\\oint_C (P\\,dx + Q\\,dy) = \\iint_R \\left(\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} - \\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}\\right) dA$.\n2. Here $P = y^2$, $Q = x^2$. So $\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} - \\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = 2x - 2y$.\n3. Region $R$: triangle with $0\\leq x\\leq 1$, $0\\leq y\\leq x$.\n4. $\\iint_R (2x-2y)\\,dA = \\int_0^1\\int_0^x (2x-2y)\\,dy\\,dx = \\int_0^1 [2xy - y^2]_0^x dx = \\int_0^1 (2x^2 - x^2)dx = \\int_0^1 x^2\\,dx = \\frac{1}{3}$."
