        "answerKey": "1. First Green's formula: $\\iiint_V (u\\nabla^2v + \\nabla u\\cdot\\nabla v)\\,dV = \\iint_{\\partial V} u\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial n}\\,dS$.\n2. Second Green's formula (Green's identity): $\\iiint_V (u\\nabla^2v - v\\nabla^2u)\\,dV = \\iint_{\\partial V}\\left(u\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial n} - v\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial n}\\right)dS$.\n3. Uniqueness proof: Suppose $u_1, u_2$ both solve the problem. Let $w = u_1 - u_2$. Then $\\nabla^2 w = 0$ in $V$, $w = 0$ on $\\partial V$.\n4. Apply first formula with $u=v=w$: $\\iiint_V |\\nabla w|^2\\,dV = \\iint_{\\partial V} w\\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial n}\\,dS = 0$ (since $w=0$ on boundary).\n5. So $\\nabla w = \\mathbf{0}$ in $V$, hence $w = $ constant $= 0$ (from boundary). Therefore $u_1 = u_2$."
